## How `MultiPlotLayer` Fits In: Time Animation

Once your product suites support time-varying data, `MultiPlotLayer` slots cleanly into `make_layers()`. The product suite builds the multi-layer; `main.js` receives a handle to drive `setActiveKey()`:

```javascript name=src/products_timevary_example.js
// Example of how a time-varying product suite would work
'gfs_500mb_animated': {
    label: '500mb Heights (GFS Animated)',
    group: 'basic',
    available_for: ['GFS'],
    async make_layers_multi(dataByFhr, grid) {
        // dataByFhr = { '000': {hght, u, v}, '006': {hght, u, v}, ... }

        const fill_layer  = new apgl.MultiPlotLayer('500_fill');
        const cntr_layer  = new apgl.MultiPlotLayer('500_cntr');
        const barb_layer  = new apgl.MultiPlotLayer('500_barbs');

        for (const [fhr, data] of Object.entries(dataByFhr)) {
            const hght_field = new apgl.RawScalarField(grid, data.hght);
            const wind_field = new apgl.RawVectorField(grid, data.u, data.v, { relative_to: 'grid' });
            // compute wspd...
            fill_layer.addField(new apgl.ContourFill(wspd_field, { cmap: COLORMAPS['pw_speed500mb'] }), fhr);
            cntr_layer.addField(new apgl.Contour(hght_field, { interval: 6 }), fhr);
            barb_layer.addField(new apgl.Barbs(wind_field, { thin_fac: 16 }), fhr);
        }

        // Return layers AND a controller to set the active time
        const setTime = (fhr) => {
            fill_layer.setActiveKey(fhr);
            cntr_layer.setActiveKey(fhr);
            barb_layer.setActiveKey(fhr);
        };

        return {
            layers: [fill_layer, cntr_layer, barb_layer],
            colorbar: [/* ... */],
            setTime,  // UI can call this from a time slider
        };
    },
},
```

