## The Key Change: `products/` becomes a directory, not a file

Instead of one giant `products.js`, you split by **group** — exactly mirroring how NMAP2's `mod_res.tbl` groups restore files. Each file is independently maintainable and maps directly to an operational forecaster's mental model.

```
src/products/
├── index.js           ← barrel: imports all groups, re-exports PRODUCT_SUITES
├── basic.js           ← temperature, heights, winds, dewpoint
├── instability.js     ← CAPE, CIN, LI, STP, SCP, EHI
├── moisture.js        ← PWat, RH, specific humidity
├── shear.js           ← bulk shear, SRH, hodograph-related
├── precipitation.js   ← QPF, snowfall, PTYPE
├── lift.js            ← lifted index, K-index, TT
├── composite.js       ← HREF paintball, SPC composites
├── raster.js          ← MRMS, satellite imagery
└── point.js           ← surface obs station models
```

Each file has the **same shape** — it exports a plain object of product suite definitions — and `index.js` merges them all:

```javascript name=src/products/index.js
