## The Concept Map: NMAP2 → web-NMAP

Here is the consolidated, updated translation table:

| NMAP2 File / Concept | web-NMAP Equivalent | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `datatype.tbl` | `src/config/datasources.js` | Format is now `'zarr'` or `'compressed_json'` instead of GEMPAK file paths |
| `mod_res.tbl` (group + availability columns) | `src/config/views.js` | Maps group names + model availability to product IDs |
| Restore file (e.g. `gfs_500mb.nmap2`) | One entry in `src/products/basic.js` | One JS object per product; grouped by file |
| `prmlst.tbl` | `src/config/stationmodels.js` | Named station model configs, referenced by `point.js` products |
| Colormap table files | `src/config/colormaps.js` | Named `ColorMap` objects, re-used across product files |
| GEMPAK binary grid file | Zarr store (`.zarr/` directory or URL) | One store per model run; variables are arrays inside |
| GEMPAK surface file (SFCOA, etc.) | Compressed JSON (`.json.gz`) | Array of obs objects, gzip'd |
| NMAP2 "restore group" | `products/*.js` file | `basic.js`, `instability.js`, etc. — one file per group |
| NMAP2 panel | `VIEW_REGISTRY` entry in `views.js` | Combines source + product + time into a renderable unit |
| `MultiPlotLayer.setActiveKey()` | Time slider in `ViewManager.js` | Drives frame stepping across forecast hours |

