## One Important Design Rule to Emphasize

The reason this decomposition works cleanly is a strict **separation of concerns** enforced by this rule:

> **Product files (`products/*.js`) know about autumnplot-gl and colormaps, but know NOTHING about data fetching, URLs, or time.**  
> **`DataLoader.js` knows about URLs and formats, but knows NOTHING about autumnplot-gl rendering.**  
> **`views.js` connects the two, but contains no rendering or fetching logic itself.**

This is exactly what NMAP2's table separation achieved in C/Fortran — and it's what prevents your codebase from collapsing into one giant `main.js` again as you add dozens of products and data sources.

